1. Calculating the average is done by adding the values and dividing by the total number of values which, in this case, is 3. 2. Southlandia is -48 degrees, Northlandia is 21 degrees, and Midlandia is -3 degrees. 3. We sum the values to get -48 + 21 + (-3) = -30. 4. We divide the sum by 3 to get -30/3 = -10.

Therefore, the average highest temperature of these 3 countries is -10 degrees Fahrenheit.

